<div class="glass card act" id="action-db-assert" style="grid-column: 1 / -1">
      <div class="act-title">🗄 DB assert — read-only, SELECT-only assertion against a database</div>
      <div class="d" style="margin-bottom:8px">Needs a second gate — <code>ZYVOR_DB_TESTING_ENABLED=true</code> — and <code>ZYVOR_SANDBOX_DB_IMAGE</code> configured server-side. Deterministic, not LLM-generated — the query runs verbatim via a fixed script (SELECT-only, enforced server-side). <b>The connection string must reference a server-side env var — the value is never sent</b>, only the env var <i>name</i>.</div>
      <div class="act-row">
        <select class="inp" id="dba-engine" style="max-width:130px">
          <option value="postgres">postgres</option>
          <option value="mysql">mysql</option>
          <option value="sqlite">sqlite</option>
        </select>
        <input class="inp grow" id="dba-target" placeholder="target label for engagement scope, e.g. staging-orders-db">
